<section class="tk-hero"><div class="tk-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="tk-w tk-hero-g"><div class="tk-hero-t"><p class="tk-code">&gt; listening to the movement_</p><h1>Every second,<br>counted <em>eight</em> times.</h1><p class="tk-lead">Ticking is an independent guide to the heartbeat of a watch: how an escapement turns a spring into seconds, what beat rate means, and how to measure whether your watch keeps good time.</p><div class="tk-hero-a"><a class="tk-btn" href="#beat">Hear the beat</a><a class="tk-btn tk-btn-o" href="#drift">Check accuracy</a></div></div>
<div class="tk-hero-v"><figure class="tk-hero-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1769971361854-9e0927a2d8dc?auto=format&fit=crop&w=620&h=460&q=75" alt="intricate metal gears and mechanical parts in close up" width="620" height="460" fetchpriority="high"></figure><div class="tk-scope"><div class="tk-scope-h"><code>CH1 &middot; acoustic</code><code class="tk-rec">&#9679; REC</code></div><svg viewBox="0 0 600 120" class="tk-wave" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 60H70L76 20L82 100L88 40L94 60H220L226 30L232 92L238 52L244 60H370L376 20L382 100L388 40L394 60H520L526 30L532 92L538 52L544 60H600"/></svg><div class="tk-scope-f"><code>rate +3 s/d</code><code>amp 285&deg;</code><code>beat 0.2 ms</code></div></div></div></div></section>

<section class="tk-sp"><div class="tk-w"><ol class="tk-specs stg"><li class="rv"><code>01</code><b>Escapement</b><p>Releases energy in tiny, equal steps</p></li><li class="rv"><code>02</code><b>Balance wheel</b><p>Swings back and forth at a steady rate</p></li><li class="rv"><code>03</code><b>Hairspring</b><p>Pulls the balance back to centre</p></li><li class="rv"><code>04</code><b>Mainspring</b><p>Stores the energy, wound by hand or rotor</p></li></ol></div></section>

<section class="tk-s tk-bt" id="beat"><div class="tk-w tk-bt-g"><div class="tk-bt-v"><svg viewBox="0 0 200 200" class="tk-dial" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="100" cy="100" r="98" class="bz"/><circle cx="100" cy="100" r="94" class="fc"/><path d="M100.0 8.0L100.0 20.0" class="mj"/><path d="M109.6 8.5L109.0 14.5" class="mn"/><path d="M119.1 10.0L117.9 15.9" class="mn"/><path d="M128.4 12.5L126.6 18.2" class="mn"/><path d="M137.4 16.0L135.0 21.4" class="mn"/><path d="M146.0 20.3L140.0 30.7" class="mj"/><path d="M154.1 25.6L150.5 30.4" class="mn"/><path d="M161.6 31.6L157.5 36.1" class="mn"/><path d="M168.4 38.4L163.9 42.5" class="mn"/><path d="M174.4 45.9L169.6 49.5" class="mn"/><path d="M179.7 54.0L169.3 60.0" class="mj"/><path d="M184.0 62.6L178.6 65.0" class="mn"/><path d="M187.5 71.6L181.8 73.4" class="mn"/><path d="M190.0 80.9L184.1 82.1" class="mn"/><path d="M191.5 90.4L185.5 91.0" class="mn"/><path d="M192.0 100.0L180.0 100.0" class="mj"/><path d="M191.5 109.6L185.5 109.0" class="mn"/><path d="M190.0 119.1L184.1 117.9" class="mn"/><path d="M187.5 128.4L181.8 126.6" class="mn"/><path d="M184.0 137.4L178.6 135.0" class="mn"/><path d="M179.7 146.0L169.3 140.0" class="mj"/><path d="M174.4 154.1L169.6 150.5" class="mn"/><path d="M168.4 161.6L163.9 157.5" class="mn"/><path d="M161.6 168.4L157.5 163.9" class="mn"/><path d="M154.1 174.4L150.5 169.6" class="mn"/><path d="M146.0 179.7L140.0 169.3" class="mj"/><path d="M137.4 184.0L135.0 178.6" class="mn"/><path d="M128.4 187.5L126.6 181.8" class="mn"/><path d="M119.1 190.0L117.9 184.1" class="mn"/><path d="M109.6 191.5L109.0 185.5" class="mn"/><path d="M100.0 192.0L100.0 180.0" class="mj"/><path d="M90.4 191.5L91.0 185.5" class="mn"/><path d="M80.9 190.0L82.1 184.1" class="mn"/><path d="M71.6 187.5L73.4 181.8" class="mn"/><path d="M62.6 184.0L65.0 178.6" class="mn"/><path d="M54.0 179.7L60.0 169.3" class="mj"/><path d="M45.9 174.4L49.5 169.6" class="mn"/><path d="M38.4 168.4L42.5 163.9" class="mn"/><path d="M31.6 161.6L36.1 157.5" class="mn"/><path d="M25.6 154.1L30.4 150.5" class="mn"/><path d="M20.3 146.0L30.7 140.0" class="mj"/><path d="M16.0 137.4L21.4 135.0" class="mn"/><path d="M12.5 128.4L18.2 126.6" class="mn"/><path d="M10.0 119.1L15.9 117.9" class="mn"/><path d="M8.5 109.6L14.5 109.0" class="mn"/><path d="M8.0 100.0L20.0 100.0" class="mj"/><path d="M8.5 90.4L14.5 91.0" class="mn"/><path d="M10.0 80.9L15.9 82.1" class="mn"/><path d="M12.5 71.6L18.2 73.4" class="mn"/><path d="M16.0 62.6L21.4 65.0" class="mn"/><path d="M20.3 54.0L30.7 60.0" class="mj"/><path d="M25.6 45.9L30.4 49.5" class="mn"/><path d="M31.6 38.4L36.1 42.5" class="mn"/><path d="M38.4 31.6L42.5 36.1" class="mn"/><path d="M45.9 25.6L49.5 30.4" class="mn"/><path d="M54.0 20.3L60.0 30.7" class="mj"/><path d="M62.6 16.0L65.0 21.4" class="mn"/><path d="M71.6 12.5L73.4 18.2" class="mn"/><path d="M80.9 10.0L82.1 15.9" class="mn"/><path d="M90.4 8.5L91.0 14.5" class="mn"/><g class="sec" id="bt-h"><path d="M100 118V14"/><circle cx="100" cy="100" r="5"/></g></svg><p class="tk-bt-c"><code id="bt-hz">4 Hz</code> &middot; <code id="bt-ps">8 ticks / second</code></p></div>
<div><p class="tk-code">// tool 01</p><h2 class="rv">Beat rate visualiser</h2><p class="tk-p">Mechanical watches are rated in beats per hour. More beats make a smoother seconds hand and slightly better stability, at the cost of faster wear. Pick a rate and watch the hand step.</p>
<div class="tk-bph" id="bt-s" role="group" aria-label="Beats per hour"><button type="button" data-v="18000"><b>18,000</b><span>2.5 Hz</span></button><button type="button" data-v="21600"><b>21,600</b><span>3 Hz</span></button><button type="button" data-v="28800" class="on"><b>28,800</b><span>4 Hz</span></button><button type="button" data-v="36000"><b>36,000</b><span>5 Hz</span></button></div><dl class="tk-read" aria-live="polite"><div><dt>Beats per second</dt><dd id="bt-b">8</dd></div><div><dt>Each beat</dt><dd id="bt-m">125 ms</dd></div><div><dt>Beats per day</dt><dd id="bt-d">691,200</dd></div></dl><p class="tk-small" id="bt-n"></p><figure class="tk-bt-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1616723824685-30ca03b667f7?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=220&q=75" alt="a silver and black analog wristwatch" width="560" height="220" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div></section>

<section class="tk-s tk-dr" id="drift"><div class="tk-w tk-dr-g"><div><p class="tk-code">// tool 02</p><h2 class="rv">Accuracy tracker</h2><p class="tk-p">Set your watch to an accurate reference clock, then check it a few days later. Enter how many seconds it gained or lost and how many days passed.</p>
<label class="tk-lb" for="dr-s">Seconds gained (+) or lost (&minus;): <b id="dr-sv">+12</b></label><input type="range" id="dr-s" min="-60" max="60" value="12" class="tk-rng">
<label class="tk-lb" for="dr-d">Days since you set it: <b id="dr-dv">3</b></label><input type="range" id="dr-d" min="1" max="30" value="3" class="tk-rng">
<p class="tk-lb">Movement</p><div class="tk-seg" id="dr-m" role="group" aria-label="Movement type"><button type="button" data-v="0" class="on">Mechanical</button><button type="button" data-v="1">Quartz</button></div></div>
<div class="tk-dr-r" aria-live="polite"><p class="tk-code">Rate</p><p class="tk-big"><span id="dr-r">+4.0</span><small>s/day</small></p><div class="tk-scale"><div class="tk-scale-b"><i class="z1"></i><i class="z2"></i><i class="z3"></i><b id="dr-p"></b></div><div class="tk-scale-k"><span>&minus;30</span><span>0</span><span>+30</span></div></div><p id="dr-v" class="tk-dr-v"></p><dl class="tk-read tk-read-s"><div><dt>Per month</dt><dd id="dr-mo"></dd></div><div><dt>Per year</dt><dd id="dr-y"></dd></div></dl><figure class="tk-dr-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1548171838-1fd4cb4ab854?auto=format&fit=crop&w=480&h=200&q=75" alt="a round silver chronograph watch" width="480" height="200" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div></section>

<section class="tk-s tk-th"><div class="tk-w"><div class="tk-sh"><p class="tk-code">// field recordings</p><h2 class="rv">Things that tick (and one that doesn&rsquo;t)</h2></div><ul class="tk-th-l stg"><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1568315112393-237808cc579c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=380&q=75" alt="a wooden anchor-shaped pendulum clock" width="300" height="380" loading="lazy"></figure><b>Pendulum</b><code>~1 tick/sec</code></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1763357515661-1fc729dcc0f0?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=380&q=75" alt="an antique cuckoo clock hanging on a wall" width="300" height="380" loading="lazy"></figure><b>Cuckoo</b><code>Weights &amp; bellows</code></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1769874827520-8eeddf779a3f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=380&q=75" alt="a tall wooden grandfather clock with a detailed face" width="300" height="380" loading="lazy"></figure><b>Longcase</b><code>2-second swing</code></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1550534791-2677533605ab?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=380&q=75" alt="a red and beige twin bell alarm clock held in a hand" width="300" height="380" loading="lazy"></figure><b>Alarm clock</b><code>Loud and fast</code></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1769029256458-fe3164fe4745?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=380&q=75" alt="a wooden hourglass held against a black background" width="300" height="380" loading="lazy"></figure><b>Hourglass</b><code>Silent, no tick</code></li></ul></div></section>

